  description:
  - Of all the flora to undergo rampid mutations, the Mandrake had the most drastic.
    The most notable of these changes include the ability to manuever on its own
    and limited sentience.
  - While most depictions paint these creatures in a playful and mischievous light,
    it is highly likely that their erratic behavior and ceaceless screaming stems
    from a psychotic break caused by their newfound consciousness.
  leftText: 
  rightText: Of all the flora to undergo rampid mutations, the Mandrake had the most
    drastic. The most notable of these changes include the ability to manuever on
    its own and limited sentience. While most depictions paint these creatures in
    a playful and mischievous light, it is highly likely that their erratic behavior
    and ceaceless screaming stems from a psychotic break caused by their newfound
    consciousness.
